    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever\n Injured and missing the entire 2022 season outside of 3 innings.\n Knee injury so should not affect his arm.\n Throws triple digits regularly. Has been up to 103 in games.\n Slider flashes being a really solid secondary and he actually commands this a decent amount better than the fastball.\n Changeup is a distant third pitch right now, would do well to make it decent enough to keep hitters honest.\n Command and control are both big concerns. The fastball moves a ton, along with the velo, which doesn't help.\n Potential to be a high leverage reliever, but command needs improvement.\n Likely a middle innings guy right now, but would give the Brewers something their pen lacks (big time velo).\n Getting Statcast data from AFL appearances now. Showing that his fastball has a ton of sink. A comparable pitch to Adrian Houser, but in the 98-101 range in MPH.\n Slider is being classified as a cutter, but seems extremely similar to Andres Munoz of the Mariners, which is classified as a slider.\n Getting really good results in the AFL, throwing a lot of strikes. Moved him back up in my rankings. Brewers will need to protect him this offseason.",
